{
 "title": "Don't Think of a White Bear",
 "scenes": [
  {
   "id": "short",
   "tail": 0.2,
   "beats": [
    {
     "id": "b00",
     "say": "Don't think of a white bear."
    },
    {
     "id": "b01",
     "say": "Don't."
    },
    {
     "id": "b02",
     "say": "Too late, right?"
    },
    {
     "id": "b03",
     "say": "In nineteen eighty-seven, psychologist Daniel Wegner tried this on students."
    },
    {
     "id": "b04",
     "say": "They talked out loud for five minutes."
    },
    {
     "id": "b05",
     "say": "One rule."
    },
    {
     "id": "b06",
     "say": "Don't think of a white bear."
    },
    {
     "id": "b07",
     "say": "Every time it popped up, they rang a bell."
    },
    {
     "id": "b08",
     "say": "Ding."
    },
    {
     "id": "b09",
     "say": "Ding."
    },
    {
     "id": "b10",
     "say": "Ding."
    },
    {
     "id": "b11",
     "say": "And when the rule ended, the bear came back even more."
    },
    {
     "id": "b12",
     "say": "Fighting a thought keeps it alive."
    },
    {
     "id": "b13",
     "say": "Same with an ex."
    },
    {
     "id": "b14",
     "say": "Or that awkward thing you said."
    },
    {
     "id": "b15",
     "say": "But one trick helped."
    },
    {
     "id": "b16",
     "say": "Pick a different thought on purpose."
    },
    {
     "id": "b17",
     "say": "In the study, it was a red car."
    },
    {
     "id": "b18",
     "say": "So picture a red car."
    },
    {
     "id": "b19",
     "say": "And whatever you do, don't think of a white bear."
    }
   ],
